  "result": "Done! Added payment terms to invoices with automatic due date calculation.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **Payment terms in createInvoice()** \u2014 Optional `terms` parameter:\n   - `'NET14'`: Due 14 days after issue date\n   - `'NET30'`: Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n   - `'EOM'`: Due on the last day of the issue date's month\n   - Unknown terms return TERMS_INVALID error\n\n2. **calculateDueDate()** \u2014 In src/dates.js:\n   - Calculates due date based on terms and issue date\n   - Handles month/year boundaries correctly\n   - Works in UTC\n   - Returns `null` for unknown terms\n\n3. **Invoice structure updated**:\n   - Every invoice now has `terms` and `dueDate` fields\n   - Preserved through addLine, removeLine, and issueInvoice\n   - Example: `terms: 'NET30', dueDate: '2026-11-06'` for issue date 2026-10-07\n\n4. **Test coverage** \u2014 15 new tests:\n   - NET14, NET30, EOM term calculations\n   - Default to NET30\n   - Month/year boundaries\n   - Leap year February handling\n   - Last day of month for various months\n   - Invalid terms rejection\n   - EOM correctly handles 28, 29, 30, 31-day months\n\nAll 154 tests pass (15 new for payment terms + 139 previous).\n\n**Invoice payment terms examples:**\n- Issue: 2026-10-07, NET14 \u2192 Due: 2026-10-21 (14 days)\n- Issue: 2026-10-07, NET30 \u2192 Due: 2026-11-06 (30 days)\n- Issue: 2026-10-15, EOM \u2192 Due: 2026-10-31 (end of October)\n- Issue: 2025-02-15, EOM \u2192 Due: 2025-02-28 (end of February, non-leap)\n- Issue: 2024-02-15, EOM \u2192 Due: 2024-02-29 (end of February, leap year)",
